{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Native Hybrid (native shell, web editor): Best when platform-native menus, shortcuts, and window behavior matter. You can reuse the editor across platforms, but you’ll maintain more platform-specific code."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tauri (system webview, Rust backend): A good fit for a lightweight, local-first workspace. Installers are typically smaller than Electron’s, but test rich editing, clipboard behavior, and keyboard shortcuts across OS webviews."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Electron (bundled Chromium, Node.js): A good fit when consistent editor behavior across platforms and a mature ecosystem matter most. The trade-off is typically larger installers and higher baseline memory use."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Start with Tauri if footprint is the priority, Electron if editor consistency is, or Native Hybrid if deep OS integration defines the experience."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Adjust the three weights independently. Each criterion’s share is its weight divided by the total, so the weights don’t need to add up to 100. If all three weights are zero, the ranking is blank."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Synthetic scores, in order: native experience, lightweight runtime, delivery efficiency. Native Hybrid: 9, 8, 7. Tauri: 7, 8, 8. Electron: 6, 4, 10."
    },
    {
      "type": "ui",
      "source": "root = Stack([nativeWeight, runtimeWeight, deliveryWeight, weightTotal, rankingLabel, ranking])\n$native = 40\n$runtime = 25\n$delivery = 35\nnativeWeight = Control(\"Native experience (weight points)\", 0, 100, [], $native)\nruntimeWeight = Control(\"Lightweight runtime (weight points)\", 0, 100, [], $runtime)\ndeliveryWeight = Control(\"Delivery efficiency (weight points)\", 0, 100, [], $delivery)\ntotal = @Sum([$native, $runtime, $delivery])\nweightTotal = Metric(\"Total weight points\", total)\ndivisor = total == 0 ? 1 : total\nhybridScore = ($native * 9 + $runtime * 8 + $delivery * 7) / divisor\ntauriScore = ($native * 7 + $runtime * 8 + $delivery * 8) / divisor\nelectronScore = ($native * 6 + $runtime * 4 + $delivery * 10) / divisor\nrows = [{label:\"Native Hybrid\",score:hybridScore},{label:\"Tauri\",score:tauriScore},{label:\"Electron\",score:electronScore}]\nrankedRows = total == 0 ? [] : @Sort(rows, \"score\", \"desc\")\nrankingLabel = Text(\"Ranking by weighted score (highest first)\")\nranking = Table(rankedRows)",
      "state": []
    }
  ]
}

{
  "version": "2b1",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tauri is the best starting point at the selected weights. Native experience has zero weight; lightweight runtime gets about 42% and delivery efficiency about 58%. On the synthetic scores, Tauri ranks first (8.00), followed by Electron (7.50) and Native Hybrid (7.42). Tauri’s runtime advantage outweighs Electron’s delivery advantage."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tauri uses the system webview, which helps keep the installer small but means editor behavior can vary by OS. Electron bundles Chromium, giving the editor a more consistent environment and a mature ecosystem at the cost of a larger installer and typically higher baseline memory use. Native Hybrid pairs a reusable web editor with a native shell for deeper OS integration, but requires more platform-specific maintenance. Its strongest criterion scores highest of the three, but that criterion is currently weighted at zero."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Prototype the editor in Tauri first. Test rich editing, clipboard behavior, and keyboard shortcuts on each target OS. If webview differences cost too much engineering time, revisit Electron. If native menus and window behavior become central to the workspace, give native experience a nonzero weight and reassess Native Hybrid. The scores are synthetic, so use the ranking to guide the prototype, not as a benchmark."
    }
  ]
}

